{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>A talent of gold.</b> Rashi's comment: a common talent is sixty maneh, a sacred one is doubled — one hundred twenty maneh. And the maneh is the litra with which silver is weighed, of the weight of Cologne; it is one hundred gold coins. So the menorah and its lamps were fifty gold litrin, according to the common reckoning that puts two hundred and forty plain coins in a litra. But the rest of its vessels were not included in the talent, as the Sages said."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:32.177173386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}